  "final_message": "I haven't made the change, because something does still read `channel`. The analytics-ingest team's repo (read-only here) requires it on `OrderPlaced`.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** parses the event with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing `channel` makes it throw `ContractViolationError`, and the whole event is rejected.\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17`** copies `channel` into the `orders` table, which has a `channel` column. Its README (lines 27 and 31) documents `channel` as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract.\n- **billing-service** doesn't need it. Its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` already handles a missing `channel`.\n\nIf I removed `channel` from the event now, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event once this was deployed. Its reports would stop updating.\n\nInside orders-service, `channel` appears in these places:\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/core/order.ts`, including the `CHANNELS` validation\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests and helpers\n- the README and CLAUDE.md examples\n\nRemoving it from the order model would also change `POST /orders`. Clients that send `channel` would no longer have it validated, and an invalid one would stop returning 400.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if analytics-ingest is being changed first or at the same time.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and the API, but keep it on the event.** That isn't possible without the model holding a value, so it isn't really an option.\n3. **Hold off** until the analytics-ingest team has dropped the requirement.\n\nTell me which one and I'll make the change. If it's option 1, I'll also update the docs and run `npm test`, `npm run arch` and `npm run typecheck`.",
